WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.036 --> 00:00:16.456
loved her star crown.

2
00:00:17.516 --> 00:00:21.277
She couldn't wait to wear it in Willow Creek's big birthday parade.

3
00:00:22.338 --> 00:00:25.899
But now she wanted day two of day camp to be finished.

4
00:00:26.979 --> 00:00:28.599
The Earthworms had work to do!

5
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.553
Finally it was eleven o'clock.

6
00:00:32.053 --> 00:00:33.933
Mrs. Penkov blew her whistle.

7
00:00:33.954 --> 00:00:36.755
"That's all for today, kids!"

8
00:00:37.215 --> 00:00:38.235
the camp leader said.

9
00:00:38.255 --> 00:00:41.557
"Please leave your hats and crowns on the shelf!"

10
00:00:41.577 --> 00:00:46.519
"Let's go, team," Katie said and headed for the door.

11
00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:51.601
Soon the Earthworms stood on the sidewalk outside the community center.

12
00:00:52.681 --> 00:00:54.702
Katie pulled open their shopping bag.

13
00:00:54.722 --> 00:00:57.803
"Look inside," she said.

14
00:00:58.363 --> 00:00:59.504
The Earthworms looked.

15
00:01:00.772 --> 00:01:03.254
"I don't see anything," said AJ.

16
00:01:03.274 --> 00:01:06.435
"Exactly," said Katie.

17
00:01:06.455 --> 00:01:07.696
"It's empty.

18
00:01:08.136 --> 00:01:10.037
The Earthworms are not doing well."

19
00:01:11.178 --> 00:01:13.259
Emily looked at the scavenger hunt list.

20
00:01:13.279 --> 00:01:15.820
"We need a menu," she said.

21
00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.022
"That's easy," said Luke.

22
00:01:19.582 --> 00:01:21.603
They headed for Fried Pie Heaven.

23
00:01:21.623 --> 00:01:25.686
"Sure, you can have a menu," said Aunt Sally.

24
00:01:25.706 --> 00:01:29.528
"But you're not the first team to come hunting here.

25
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:32.221
Don't ask me who came though.

26
00:01:32.762 --> 00:01:33.722
I won't tell!"

27
00:01:34.743 --> 00:01:35.824
Aunt Sally laughed.

28
00:01:36.384 --> 00:01:37.885
The Earthworms frowned.

29
00:01:39.426 --> 00:01:41.427
Next they went to the post office.

30
00:01:41.447 --> 00:01:45.810
"Let me guess," said Pete, the post office clerk.

31
00:01:47.011 --> 00:01:47.812
"Not stamps.

32
00:01:48.192 --> 00:01:49.133
Not a postcard.

33
00:01:49.613 --> 00:01:51.815
You want a change-of-address form."

34
00:01:51.835 --> 00:01:53.716
"How did you know?"

35
00:01:54.216 --> 00:01:54.937
asked Emily.

36
00:01:54.957 --> 00:01:59.420
"Some scavengers came by yesterday," said Pete.

37
00:02:01.128 --> 00:02:03.070
"Rats!" said AJ.

38
00:02:04.191 --> 00:02:06.293
The Earthworms ran to the library.

39
00:02:06.313 --> 00:02:11.137
"We can get a calendar of community events here," said Katie.

40
00:02:11.157 --> 00:02:12.978
"Oh, look!"

41
00:02:13.539 --> 00:02:16.021
said Debra Donovan when they came through the door.

42
00:02:16.041 --> 00:02:17.882
"More scavengers!"

43
00:02:19.484 --> 00:02:21.025
The Earthworms groaned.

44
00:02:22.146 --> 00:02:26.449
The team left the library and walked slowly back down Main Street.

45
00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:29.392
They had three things in their bag.

46
00:02:30.464 --> 00:02:33.447
But it seemed like all the other teams were beating them.

47
00:02:35.108 --> 00:02:39.672
They crossed Walnut Street and came to Henderson's Gas Station and Auto Shop.

48
00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.034
Emily looked at the list.

49
00:02:42.054 --> 00:02:44.015
"Maybe Mr.

50
00:02:44.055 --> 00:02:47.838
Henderson has a pen with his business name printed on it," she said.

51
00:02:47.858 --> 00:02:50.200
"Anybody there?"

52
00:02:50.721 --> 00:02:51.401
Luke called.

53
00:02:51.421 --> 00:02:53.463
"I'm back here!"

54
00:02:54.003 --> 00:02:54.684
answered Mr.

55
00:02:54.724 --> 00:02:56.926
Henderson. "Come on in!"

56
00:02:56.946 --> 00:03:00.744
"Wow!" said AJ.

57
00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:03.045
"Look at that old car!"

58
00:03:03.065 --> 00:03:07.207
"This is a Model T Ford," said Mr.

59
00:03:07.247 --> 00:03:08.407
Henderson proudly.

60
00:03:08.427 --> 00:03:11.769
"The car that put America on wheels!

61
00:03:12.369 --> 00:03:13.750
And this is my grandpa."

62
00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.471
A very old man was wiping one of the car doors.

63
00:03:18.491 --> 00:03:22.573
"Grandpa Henderson found this car in an old barn.

64
00:03:23.654 --> 00:03:26.475
We've been working for two years to make it look like new."

65
00:03:26.495 --> 00:03:29.576
"Cool," said Emily.

66
00:03:30.972 --> 00:03:32.973
"Excellent!" said Luke.

67
00:03:32.993 --> 00:03:37.015
"But it's not on our list," thought Katie.

68
00:03:37.035 --> 00:03:41.818
"We're getting it ready for Willow Creek's birthday parade," said Mr.

69
00:03:41.838 --> 00:03:46.381
Henderson. "We're going to be in the parade too!"

70
00:03:46.881 --> 00:03:47.641
said AJ.

71
00:03:47.661 --> 00:03:54.005
"We think this was the first automobile in Willow Creek," said Grandpa Henderson.

72
00:03:54.025 --> 00:03:57.327
"It was made in 1920.

73
00:03:57.867 --> 00:03:59.608
It's almost as old as I am!"

74
00:04:00.916 --> 00:04:01.877
"How old are you?"

75
00:04:02.377 --> 00:04:02.977
asked Luke.

76
00:04:02.997 --> 00:04:05.338
"I'm 92."

77
00:04:05.358 --> 00:04:10.081
"You must be the oldest person in Willow Creek!"

78
00:04:10.681 --> 00:04:11.382
said Katie.

79
00:04:11.402 --> 00:04:15.324
"No, I'm not," he said, laughing.

80
00:04:15.344 --> 00:04:17.265
"But you know who is?

81
00:04:18.065 --> 00:04:20.547
My sister, Cora Mae Henderson!

82
00:04:21.067 --> 00:04:24.008
She is 103 years old."

83
00:04:24.028 --> 00:04:26.990
"One hundred three!"

84
00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:28.211
cried Katie.

85
00:04:28.231 --> 00:04:30.532
"This could be our big chance!"

86
00:04:31.732 --> 00:04:33.192
The Earthworms told Mr.

87
00:04:33.232 --> 00:04:36.373
Henderson and his grandpa about the scavenger hunt.

88
00:04:37.594 --> 00:04:39.694
"Have any other scavengers been here?"

89
00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:40.895
asked Emily.

90
00:04:40.915 --> 00:04:44.716
"No," said Grandpa Henderson.

91
00:04:44.736 --> 00:04:47.436
"Great!" said Katie.

92
00:04:47.456 --> 00:04:49.537
"We have to meet your sister."

93
00:04:49.557 --> 00:04:55.078
"Well, that could be a problem," said the old man.

94
00:04:55.098 --> 00:04:57.219
"She never comes to town."

95
00:04:57.239 --> 00:04:59.880
"We can go visit her!"

96
00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:00.700
said Katie.

97
00:05:02.332 --> 00:05:06.457
"Hmm She doesn't like a lot of visitors," he said.

98
00:05:06.477 --> 00:05:08.339
"But you could try."

99
00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:13.265
He pulled a notepad from his pocket and started drawing a map.

100
00:05:13.285 --> 00:05:17.971
"First, you go way out to the end of Old Church Road
